### Task Manager — Project CRUD
# IntelliJ ships an HTTP client: click the green ▶ next to each request.
# Run the app first:  mvn spring-boot:run   (needs `docker compose up -d`)
#
# Check the STATUS CODE, not just the body:
#   create → 201    get/list/update → 200    delete → 204
#   validation error → 400    unknown id → 404    duplicate name → 409

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Create a project  → 201 Created
POST {{host}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Interview prep",
  "description": "24-day plan"
}

### List all projects  → 200
GET {{host}}/api/projects

### Get one project  → 200 (use an id returned above)
GET {{host}}/api/projects/73

### Update a project  → 200
PUT {{host}}/api/projects/73
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Interview prep (revised)",
  "description": "24-day plan, tightened"
}

### Delete a project  → 204 No Content
DELETE {{host}}/api/projects/73

### Validation error: blank name  → 400  { "name": "Name is required" }
POST {{host}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": ""
}

### Not found: unknown id  → 404  { "status": 404, "message": "Project 999 not found" }
GET {{host}}/api/projects/999

### Conflict: duplicate name  → 409  (run the first "Create" twice)
POST {{host}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Interview prep",
  "description": "duplicate on purpose"
}
